libdjvu/DjVuFile: fail the decoding when its thread cannot be started

DjVuFile::start_decode() sets the DECODING flag and starts a thread that runs
decode_func(), which clears it. The result of GThread::create() was ignored,
so when pthread_create() fails (EAGAIN under RLIMIT_NPROC, or no address space
left for the stack under RLIMIT_AS) the file stays DECODING forever and every
file that includes it waits in wait_for_finish(): ddjvu then waits at 0% CPU
until it is killed. A chain of 300 shared files that each include the next
does this under a 2 GiB address space limit.

Throw DjVuFile.decode_fail when the thread does not start. The handler that
is already there clears DECODING, sets DECODE_FAILED and notifies the ports,
so the including file fails as for any included file that cannot be decoded
and the program reports the error. The life saver reference that the thread
would have released is released here.

--- a/libdjvu/DjVuFile.cpp
+++ b/libdjvu/DjVuFile.cpp
@@ -1338,7 +1338,12 @@
       decode_life_saver=this;
       
       decode_thread=new GThread();
-      decode_thread->create(static_decode_func, this);
+      if (decode_thread->create(static_decode_func, this))
+      {
+        // The thread did not start: nothing will ever finish decoding.
+        decode_life_saver=0;
+        G_THROW( ERR_MSG("DjVuFile.decode_fail") );
+      }
     }
   }
   G_CATCH_ALL
